window.docContents[221].resolve({"/Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic/Worked-Examples/#Formal-Software-Verification--Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic--Worked-Examples--Disjunction-Commutes":{"contents":"Case analysis on the disjunction rebuilds it with the disjuncts exchanged.\n\n               [P]           [Q]\n   [P ∨ Q]    ─────── ∨I₂   ─────── ∨I₁\n              Q ∨ P         Q ∨ P\n  ───────────────────────────────────── ∨E\n             Q ∨ P\n  ──────────────────────  →I\n   P ∨ Q → Q ∨ P\n\n\nexample (P Q : Prop) : P ∨ Q → Q ∨ P :=\n  fun h => h.elim\n    (fun hP => Or.inr hP)\n    (fun hQ => Or.inl hQ)\n\n\nexample (P Q : Prop) : P ∨ Q → Q ∨ P := by\n  intro h\n  cases h with\n  | inl hP => exact Or.inr hP\n  | inr hQ => exact Or.inl hQ\n\n\n","context":"Formal Software Verification\u0009Lecture 1: Motivation and Propositional Logic\u0009Worked Examples","header":"1.8.4. Disjunction Commutes","id":"/Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic/Worked-Examples/#Formal-Software-Verification--Lecture-1___-Motivation-and-Propositional-Logic--Worked-Examples--Disjunction-Commutes"}});